{
  "case_id": "2016-16-54",
  "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The key statutory term of the INA in this case is the word \"abuse.\" And the Federal statute criminalizing sexual abuse of a minor, as well as the State statutes dealing with the same subject, dictate that sexual relations become abuse only -- on account of age, only when the younger partner in the activity is younger than 16."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: And you're not asking us to overrule Chevron."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So what do we do with Chevron if we think it's ambiguous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Multi-jurisdictional survey would yield age 16?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you have a federal statute. You have the Model Penal Code, which goes the same way. You have 30-plus State laws. So at the least, am I right that -- that you concede that you can't win unless Chevron applies; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allon Kedem",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The term \"sexual abuse of a minor\" would naturally support the interpretation that we offer in the first section of our brief to cover all sexual activity directed at a minor under the age of 18 years old."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So you necessarily apply Chevron before you apply the rule of lenity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KEDEM",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: I think -- I think that you do, but I think there's still work for lenity to do even after applying Chevron. Certainly, if the board has spoken to the precise question at issue, then I think it would be hard for you to be left at the end of the day after giving that deference where it's a grievous ambiguity. But often agencies speak only to a related question or fill only part of a statutory gap, in which case after giving appropriate deference to that answer, you would still possibly be left with a different aspect of the problem that you simply cannot resolve, in which case lenity would apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But why is INS in any better position to make that determination than the American Bar Association or the forest service?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KEDEM",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: So, first of all, Justice Kennedy, I think it's important to orient ourselves around the fact that this is a civil statute that's being applied in a civil context."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KEDEM",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KEDEM: So, Justice Breyer, one thing to keep in mind is that the aggravated felony definition is a spine that runs throughout the INA and determines a whole range of administrative consequences, not merely whether a person is removable, but whether they're eligible, for instance, for cancelation of removal --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: And you said one, because there's no cross-reference, so I got that one. You said two --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Mr. Kedem, Mr. Fisher said and I just want to make sure that this is right, that you no longer rely on the statute that the BIA relied on; is that correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0002-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Is it your understanding anything other than -- if a stranger does anything to a minor other than commit a rape, then that would not be sexual abuse of a minor because the person wouldn't be a relative or an acquaintance?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2016-16-54",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "7d999b607800d3b02742a24197417fc2f0beba40667fee2a265a7e78f363a904",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7d999b607800-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:07 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
    {
